<section class="si-hero"><div class="si-w si-hero-g"><div class="si-hero-t"><p class="si-kick">A journal of shape &amp; line</p><h1>The <i>shape</i><br>of things<br>to wear.</h1><p class="si-sig">silhouette first</p><p class="si-lead">Before colour, before fabric, before trend, there is the outline. Silhout is an independent guide to silhouettes and proportion: which shapes balance which, and how to find the lines that feel like you.</p><div class="si-hero-a"><a class="si-btn" href="#shape">Find your silhouette</a><a class="si-lnk" href="five-classic-silhouettes-guide.html">Read the five classics</a></div></div>
<div class="si-hero-v"><figure class="si-cut"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792588067900-e3774a3c10bc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=540&h=720&q=75" alt="the silhouette of a woman in a flowing dress walking" width="540" height="720" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="si-cut2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1786120867723-e0ac6ba8a215?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=380&q=75" alt="a woman in silhouette against a bright window" width="300" height="380" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="si-hero-f"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 420" class="si-fig si-fig-h" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="100" cy="40" r="22" class="hd"/><path class="bd" id="hf" d="M78 70Q100 64 122 70L150 92Q156 100 146 112L132 150Q128 190 136 220L172 380H28L64 220Q72 190 68 150L54 112Q44 100 50 92Z"/></svg></div><p class="si-vert" aria-hidden="true">LINE &middot; VOLUME &middot; BALANCE</p></div></div></section>

<section class="si-mq mq" aria-hidden="true"><div><span>A-line</span><i>/</i><span>Column</span><i>/</i><span>Hourglass</span><i>/</i><span>Fit &amp; flare</span><i>/</i><span>Oversized</span><i>/</i><span>Empire</span><i>/</i><span>Sheath</span><i>/</i><span>Trapeze</span><i>/</i><span>A-line</span><i>/</i><span>Column</span><i>/</i><span>Hourglass</span><i>/</i><span>Fit &amp; flare</span><i>/</i><span>Oversized</span><i>/</i><span>Empire</span><i>/</i><span>Sheath</span><i>/</i><span>Trapeze</span><i>/</i></div></section>

<section class="si-s si-gal"><div class="si-w"><div class="si-sh-h"><p class="si-kick">The lexicon</p><h2 class="rv">Four outlines, four moods</h2><p class="si-p">Scroll sideways through the shapes that shape almost every garment.</p></div></div><div class="si-rail"><figure class="si-sh rv"><div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792588192943-38393006e391?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=560&q=75" alt="a person in a flowing white dress moving against the light" width="420" height="560" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><span>01</span><b>A-line</b>Fitted at the top, flaring gently from the waist.</figcaption></figure><figure class="si-sh rv"><div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1762430816003-f3b9e00ea7c4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=560&q=75" alt="a model walking the runway in a pleated outfit" width="420" height="560" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><span>02</span><b>Column</b>One long, unbroken vertical line.</figcaption></figure><figure class="si-sh rv"><div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784850350614-5e737b4648ca?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=560&q=75" alt="a pink feathered gown on the runway" width="420" height="560" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><span>03</span><b>Ball gown</b>A defined bodice over a full, dramatic skirt.</figcaption></figure><figure class="si-sh rv"><div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1775808949670-c0dae0c0322f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=560&q=75" alt="a woman in a vintage dress under dramatic lighting" width="420" height="560" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><span>04</span><b>Fit &amp; flare</b>Close to the body, then a lively flare.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

<section class="si-s si-fd" id="shape"><div class="si-w si-fd-g"><div class="si-fd-v"><div class="si-stage"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 420" class="si-fig" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="100" cy="40" r="22" class="hd"/><path class="bd" id="fd-b" d="M78 70Q100 64 122 70L150 92Q156 100 146 112L132 150Q128 190 136 220L172 380H28L64 220Q72 190 68 150L54 112Q44 100 50 92Z"/></svg><div class="si-tape" aria-hidden="true"><i class="t1"></i><i class="t2"></i><i class="t3"></i></div></div><figure class="si-fd-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541941702428-22609a10cb9e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=240&q=75" alt="a dress form wearing a black and white outfit" width="520" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div><p class="si-kick">Tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Silhouette finder</h2><p class="si-p">Compare your shoulders, waist and hips with the sliders. The figure changes shape, and we suggest the outlines that create balance.</p>
<label class="si-lb" for="fd-s">Shoulders <b id="fd-sv">balanced</b></label><input type="range" id="fd-s" min="-2" max="2" value="0" class="si-rng">
<label class="si-lb" for="fd-w">Waist definition <b id="fd-wv">some</b></label><input type="range" id="fd-w" min="0" max="2" value="1" class="si-rng">
<label class="si-lb" for="fd-h">Hips <b id="fd-hv">balanced</b></label><input type="range" id="fd-h" min="-2" max="2" value="0" class="si-rng">
<div class="si-res" aria-live="polite"><p class="si-sig">you are</p><h3 id="fd-t">Hourglass</h3><p id="fd-d"></p><p class="si-res-k">Try</p><ul id="fd-l" class="si-tags"></ul></div></div></div></section>

<section class="si-s si-hm" id="hem"><div class="si-w si-hm-g"><div><p class="si-kick">Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Hemline &amp; proportion calculator</h2><p class="si-p">Designers often divide the body in thirds so the eye reads clothes as balanced. Enter your height to see where knee, midi and ankle hems fall, and the split that flatters most.</p>
<label class="si-lb" for="hm-h">Height <b id="hm-hv">5 ft 6 in</b></label><input type="range" id="hm-h" min="58" max="76" value="66" class="si-rng">
<p class="si-lb">Top length</p><div class="si-seg" id="hm-t" role="group" aria-label="Top length"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Tucked in</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Hip length</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Long tunic</button></div>
<dl class="si-hm-r" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Knee</dt><dd id="hm-k"></dd></div><div><dt>Midi</dt><dd id="hm-m"></dd></div><div><dt>Ankle</dt><dd id="hm-a"></dd></div></dl><p class="si-hm-n" id="hm-n"></p></div>
